@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] mirror-admin-and-reader-boundary
Repository registration, removal and manual refresh MUST recheck current
administrator authority and recent passkey elevation. Browser reads MUST
require a current stored login and a registered mirror.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] mirror-durable-state-and-audit
PostgreSQL MUST hold registration, refresh state and append-only audit outcomes.
Enrico cache state MUST NOT independently grant browser access. Failed refreshes
MUST retain the previous published head and be reconciled by Oban. An interrupted
worker MUST resume a still-running Enrico attempt; transient status failures
MUST NOT start a competing fetch. Manual refresh MUST reject a repository
already refreshing, and Oban job uniqueness MUST cover the entire job timeout.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:recovery] mirror-removal-independent-reconciliation
Removal intent MUST have a distinct durable job identity from refresh work and
MUST be reconciled while the repository is removing, regardless of its next
refresh deadline.

@cc [owner:ghuntley,label:security] mirror-verified-private-transport
Marshall MUST verify Enrico's hostname against a dedicated CA certificate.
TLS, timeout and service errors MUST be reduced to a fixed reason vocabulary
before entering audit records or structured events. Credentials and raw
transport errors MUST NOT enter the audit trail.
